--TEST--
A block with `tls = "none"` on a host `[capabilities.ldap] cleartext` grants binds over plain `ldap://`, and `whoami` returns the same identity it returns over LDAPS — `rule:security/ldap-cleartext-bind-is-granted-per-host`
--SKIPIF--
<?nvs
// The case needs the `samba-ad` server from `tests/db/compose.yaml`. Where it
// does not answer, the case is skipped, unless `NVS_LDAP_SAMBA` is set: CI's
// Linux leg runs the server and sets it, so a missing server fails there.
try {
    Core\Ldap::connect("corp");
} catch (Core\Ldap\LdapError $down) {
    if ($down->kind != Core\Ldap\LdapError::Kind::Unavailable || Core\Env::get("NVS_LDAP_SAMBA") != null) {
        throw $down;
    }
    echo "skip - ", $down->message, "\n";
}
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Ldap\Connection::whoami
// The `plain` block sends its password without TLS. Only a test server on
// this machine may be reached that way. The copied `ca.crt` is for the `corp`
// block, and the case is skipped where the test server is not running.
var $plain = Core\Ldap::connect("plain");
var $secure = Core\Ldap::connect("corp");
echo "plain: ", $plain->whoami(), "\n";
echo "same as LDAPS: ", $plain->whoami() == $secure->whoami() ? "yes" : "no", "\n";
--COPY--
../../db/ca.crt
--FILE nvs.toml--
[capabilities.ldap]
connect = ["corp", "plain"]
cleartext = ["localhost"]

[ldap.corp]
url = "ldaps://localhost:16636"
user = "CN=Administrator,CN=Users,DC=example,DC=test"
password = "Novis-test-1"
tls_ca_file = "ca.crt"

[ldap.plain]
url = "ldap://localhost:16389"
user = "CN=Administrator,CN=Users,DC=example,DC=test"
password = "Novis-test-1"
tls = "none"
--EXPECT--
plain: u:EXAMPLE\Administrator
same as LDAPS: yes
